;; What 0.31.0 renames, merges, re-means and retires, as data (docs/catalog.md, "A
;; release's renames").  `lein lint`'s E22 holds it to the changelog's Breaking entries,
;; the shipped KB and the API goldens.
;;
;; The four top-level keys are KB vocabulary, which `upgrade --sync`
;; (`vaelii.host.sync/rename!`) rewrites in stored premises (`:renames`,
;; `:context-merges`) or reports (`:re-meanings`, `:retired`).  `:api` holds the
;; same kinds for the public API, koinii's vars and the daemon's ops, which a
;; caller's code rewrites.
{:renames        {}
 :context-merges {}
 :re-meanings    {}
 :retired        #{}
 :api
 {:re-meanings {vaelii.koinii.dispute/dispute-id
                "takes (kb entry): an id is the sorted content digests of its sides"}
  :retired     #{vaelii.koinii.deref/->SentexRef
                 vaelii.koinii.deref/locator-index
                 vaelii.koinii.deref/resolve-by-locator}}}
